WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.001 --> 00:00:03.702
There are 12 of them.

00:00:05.403 --> 00:00:08.205
12 stadiums built across Europe,

00:00:10.766 --> 00:00:16.291
imagined by the most daring architects and built by thousands of workers and engineers.

00:00:20.314 --> 00:00:25.356
12 gigantic arenas selected to host matches for a global event,

00:00:25.696 --> 00:00:27.798
the 2020 European Football Championship.

00:00:31.958 --> 00:00:36.527
Embark on a unique tour of Europe to discover the most beautiful stadiums on the continent.

00:01:02.027 --> 00:01:02.829
In this episode,

00:01:03.249 --> 00:01:10.472
The match will pit the National Arena of Bucharest in Romania against the Pouchkas Arena of Budapest in Hungary.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:29.549
On one hand,

00:01:30.329 --> 00:01:32.091
an arena resembling an amphitheater,

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:34.132
equipped with a retractable roof,

00:01:34.653 --> 00:01:37.515
is designed to withstand the most powerful earthquakes.

00:01:39.877 --> 00:01:40.617
It's magnificent.

00:01:41.198 --> 00:01:41.838
From the outside,

00:01:41.878 --> 00:01:43.359
It looks like the Colosseum in Rome.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.121
And inside,

00:01:46.382 --> 00:01:47.623
We are safe from earthquakes.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:51.224
On the other hand,

00:01:51.825 --> 00:01:53.945
a newly constructed enclosure

00:01:54.587 --> 00:01:56.867
ready to become the new emblem of Hungarian sport,

00:01:57.509 --> 00:02:00.730
preserving the legendary symbols of a stadium that no longer exists.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.593
The Hungarian people loved the old stadium very much,

00:02:03.813 --> 00:02:05.073
We were all very attached to it.

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:06.174
The biggest challenge,

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:08.818
It was about figuring out how to make people love the new stadium.

00:02:08.978 --> 00:02:11.701
How could he possibly take the very special place that the old one held?

00:02:12.782 --> 00:02:14.044
Bucharest and Budapest,

00:02:14.425 --> 00:02:16.426
two stadiums located in Eastern Europe,

00:02:16.587 --> 00:02:18.610
links between the past and the future.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:42.344
Let's begin our journey in Romania and its capital,

00:02:43.085 --> 00:02:44.246
the largest city in the country,

00:02:44.647 --> 00:02:45.868
with its 2 million inhabitants.

00:02:49.914 --> 00:02:52.717
This unique city is a bridge between East and West.

00:02:55.015 --> 00:02:55.837
These wide avenues,

00:02:56.337 --> 00:02:57.778
legacy of the communist era,

00:02:58.379 --> 00:03:00.741
are dotted with gardens and magnificent parks,

00:03:01.201 --> 00:03:02.902
like Liamanoliu Park,

00:03:03.484 --> 00:03:04.905
located east of the capital,

00:03:05.306 --> 00:03:06.507
the city's green lung.

00:03:11.771 --> 00:03:12.152
This is it.

00:03:12.432 --> 00:03:13.633
in 1953,

00:03:14.213 --> 00:03:16.135
that the first national stadium was built.

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:20.420
He played a decisive role in the development of the territory.

00:03:22.148 --> 00:03:26.910
A park and sports facilities have been built all around the stadium.

00:03:28.651 --> 00:03:28.991
Today,

00:03:29.091 --> 00:03:30.472
This is Liamanoliu Park.

00:03:32.352 --> 00:03:34.213
The installation of these infrastructures,

00:03:34.353 --> 00:03:35.274
very close to the city centre,

00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:37.615
has generated a new dynamic for this area.

00:03:39.814 --> 00:03:40.915
All the surrounding neighborhoods,

00:03:40.936 --> 00:03:42.457
like Pantelimon or Titan,

00:03:42.737 --> 00:03:43.977
developed at that time.

00:03:44.537 --> 00:03:47.439
It was truly a trigger for urban growth.

00:03:51.148 --> 00:03:55.092
The historic stadium in Bucharest has hosted major sporting competitions.

00:03:55.912 --> 00:03:58.995
And over the years it has become a national institution.

00:04:02.058 --> 00:04:05.881
The old stadium from the 1950s was a flat stadium.

00:04:06.582 --> 00:04:11.126
It was very large and could accommodate well over 60,000 spectators.

00:04:12.927 --> 00:04:15.129
It also served as a performance venue.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:17.131
for people like Ceausescu,

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.571
to convey political messages.

00:04:22.031 --> 00:04:25.314
The stadium is not only located in the heart of the city of Bucharest,

00:04:26.973 --> 00:04:28.694
but also in the hearts of Romanians.

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:34.016
In 1953,

00:04:34.776 --> 00:04:38.478
The stadium is built inside a kind of crater surrounded by embankments.

00:04:42.443 --> 00:04:43.244
In the 2000s,

00:04:43.804 --> 00:04:45.226
The stadium is old and worn.

00:04:46.307 --> 00:04:51.932
The authorities then decided to completely demolish the structure in order to rebuild a new enclosure on the same site.

00:04:55.055 --> 00:05:00.000
Removing these 125,000 m3 of earth would have had a significant cost and lengthened the construction time.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.161
if it had been superior.

00:05:05.665 --> 00:05:09.908
The engineers decided to reuse the fill and integrate it into the new enclosure.

00:05:16.112 --> 00:05:20.917
They move the earth and form a 6-meter-high embankment along three-quarters of the perimeter.

00:05:22.358 --> 00:05:24.821
The three stands rest upon them,

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:25.380
north,

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.242
east and south,

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:27.382
of the new stadium.

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:31.596
The main stand,

00:05:31.656 --> 00:05:32.197
As for her,

00:05:32.657 --> 00:05:33.757
then lands lower down,

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:35.740
at the level of the arrival of the spectators.

00:05:37.099 --> 00:05:42.002
This solution prevented wasting land and also improved the spectator experience.

00:05:50.156 --> 00:05:51.278
When we arrive at the stadium,

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:52.778
We are at ground level.

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:54.119
To enter,

00:05:54.559 --> 00:05:56.980
We have to climb the stairs to reach the embankment.

00:05:57.519 --> 00:05:57.781
And then,

00:05:58.141 --> 00:05:59.321
We have a magnificent view.

00:06:01.762 --> 00:06:04.543
You can stroll around the stadium overlooking the park,

00:06:05.204 --> 00:06:06.043
6 meters above.

00:06:07.163 --> 00:06:10.045
And to enjoy what surrounds us.

00:06:18.639 --> 00:06:19.800
Upon entering the enclosure,

00:06:20.441 --> 00:06:23.542
The 63,000 spectators arrive halfway up the stands.

00:06:24.783 --> 00:06:25.043
From there,

00:06:25.703 --> 00:06:32.766
The two levels of bleachers stand out very distinctly and you can walk all around them with an unobstructed view of the entire field.

00:06:44.388 --> 00:06:48.310
But the architects and engineers didn't just work on the interior aesthetics of the stadium.

00:07:02.295 --> 00:07:03.816
With its shape and repetitions,

00:07:04.836 --> 00:07:10.319
The design of the national arena is reminiscent in many ways of a masterpiece of ancient architecture.

00:07:12.139 --> 00:07:12.780
the Colosseum.

00:07:21.817 --> 00:07:25.680
The Bucharest arena bears obvious similarities to Roman arenas.

00:07:27.281 --> 00:07:27.920
For example,

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:30.043
all the pillars,

00:07:30.403 --> 00:07:32.324
the vertical columns that support the arena,

00:07:33.504 --> 00:07:35.105
remind us of the different levels of the test.

00:07:37.408 --> 00:07:39.610
the Roman era.

00:07:39.651 --> 00:07:41.533
Other elements of the perimeter,

00:07:42.355 --> 00:07:44.957
The Bucharest arena has an oval facade.

00:07:45.017 --> 00:07:50.064
The other point of similarity is the point of similarity of the Bucharest arena.

00:07:50.063 --> 00:07:51.404
One of the biggest filling problems with the Colosseum,

00:07:51.405 --> 00:07:51.905
That's the roof.

00:07:52.365 --> 00:07:54.728
The architects installed what is called a velarium,

00:07:55.209 --> 00:07:57.151
exactly like in Roman amphitheaters.

00:07:58.392 --> 00:08:01.415
A movable sail that can be opened and closed as needed.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:19.862
The layout of the stands in the national arena echoes the slightly inclined seating of the Colosseum.

00:08:25.824 --> 00:08:28.245
But the national arena is also a contemporary stadium,

00:08:28.685 --> 00:08:30.425
as shown by the colors of its seats,

00:08:30.846 --> 00:08:33.447
which contrast sharply with the building's antique aesthetic.

00:08:51.068 --> 00:08:53.257
These colors represent the Romanian national flag.

00:08:53.678 --> 00:08:54.020
red,

00:08:54.201 --> 00:08:54.683
yellow and blue.

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:58.141
It's a stadium built by Romanians.

00:08:58.861 --> 00:08:59.561
for Romanians,

00:09:00.362 --> 00:09:02.963
Therefore, the national flag had to be present.

00:09:05.625 --> 00:09:07.126
Even when there are no spectators,

00:09:07.586 --> 00:09:09.407
The stadium seems alive.

00:09:09.467 --> 00:09:13.049
We look around and we get the impression that there are people.

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:17.531
This is one of the main reasons why the seats were colored this way.

00:09:17.932 --> 00:09:19.072
to make the stadium come alive,

00:09:19.893 --> 00:09:20.773
so that it looks inhabited.

00:09:24.251 --> 00:09:25.932
By combining tradition and modernity,

00:09:26.752 --> 00:09:31.533
The designers have succeeded in making this new building a landmark for the entire country.

00:09:35.014 --> 00:09:36.235
In the capital of Hungary,

00:09:36.615 --> 00:09:37.335
in Budapest,

00:09:38.075 --> 00:09:43.497
Another national stadium was also demolished to make way for a new one.

00:09:43.997 --> 00:09:44.997
the Puskás Arena.

00:10:03.241 --> 00:10:05.261
This city has had a tumultuous history.

00:10:06.522 --> 00:10:08.722
Budapest has a new face today.

00:10:10.143 --> 00:10:12.243
Many buildings are being restored and,

00:10:12.263 --> 00:10:13.484
like its stadium,

00:10:14.104 --> 00:10:16.084
new architectural pieces stand out.

00:10:18.985 --> 00:10:23.787
This new arena with a capacity of nearly 70,000 seats has just been completed.

00:10:32.515 --> 00:10:33.796
An extraordinary construction project.

00:10:34.397 --> 00:10:37.779
since it is the largest public building in Hungary and, above all,

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:39.961
a symbol for all the Hungarian people.

00:10:41.903 --> 00:10:44.705
The stadium is built on the same site as the legendary old stadium.

00:10:45.306 --> 00:10:45.986
Nepstadion,

00:10:46.607 --> 00:10:47.567
the people's stadium

00:10:47.988 --> 00:10:49.209
which therefore had to be destroyed.

00:10:56.475 --> 00:11:00.778
This 100,000-seat structure was inaugurated in 1953.

00:11:02.899 --> 00:11:05.541
It has been the site of the national team's greatest achievements.

00:11:06.822 --> 00:11:08.183
A legend in the history of sport,

00:11:08.584 --> 00:11:09.905
nicknamed the Golden 11,

00:11:10.565 --> 00:11:12.006
led by its star striker,

00:11:12.347 --> 00:11:13.187
Ferenc Puskas,

00:11:13.768 --> 00:11:14.869
the idol of the entire country.

00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:23.696
In Taldunay,

00:11:24.036 --> 00:11:25.757
32 caps for the Hungarian national team,

00:11:26.198 --> 00:11:27.339
remembers that time.

00:11:34.527 --> 00:11:35.588
Those were great matches.

00:11:36.268 --> 00:11:37.648
The stadium was always full.

00:11:38.669 --> 00:11:39.269
And at the time,

00:11:39.569 --> 00:11:41.569
Football was a celebration for everyone.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:44.330
There were some very great footballers,

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:46.151
like those who were part of the golden eleven.

00:11:47.091 --> 00:11:49.532
The Hungarian team won almost all of its matches.

00:11:50.132 --> 00:11:51.932
They were truly the best team in the world.

00:11:53.273 --> 00:11:55.753
The atmosphere in the stadium was truly fantastic.

00:11:56.033 --> 00:12:01.155
1954.

00:12:01.875 --> 00:12:04.557
One particularly memorable match left a lasting impression.

00:12:06.177 --> 00:12:08.759
A friendly match between Hungary and England,

00:12:09.219 --> 00:12:12.581
which ended in a 7-1 victory for the Hungarians.

00:12:16.863 --> 00:12:18.104
The stadium also hosted,

00:12:18.284 --> 00:12:19.285
repeatedly,

00:12:19.625 --> 00:12:21.086
the European Athletics Championships.

00:12:24.027 --> 00:12:25.828
Through these various sporting events,

00:12:26.429 --> 00:12:29.290
The people's stadium has become a symbol for the entire country.

00:12:32.347 --> 00:12:32.867
Over time,

00:12:33.547 --> 00:12:37.989
The structure had completely deteriorated and demolition was inevitable.

00:12:49.012 --> 00:12:53.154
The Hungarian authorities have therefore decided to rebuild on the same site a

00:12:53.194 --> 00:12:54.314
ultra-modern stadium.

00:13:09.015 --> 00:13:11.577
But they gave the designer a specific mission.

00:13:12.398 --> 00:13:15.641
To preserve the soul of the old one within this new enclosure.

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:27.911
This is Giorgis Kardély,

00:13:28.451 --> 00:13:29.872
renowned Hungarian architect,

00:13:30.573 --> 00:13:32.194
who was chosen to take on the challenge.

00:13:34.171 --> 00:13:34.871
Football fan,

00:13:35.592 --> 00:13:39.433
Giorgi often came to watch matches in the old stadium when he was a child.

00:13:46.035 --> 00:13:50.077
How can you transmit the spirit and soul of a stadium if you have to destroy it completely?

00:13:51.197 --> 00:13:51.938
To begin with,

00:13:51.939 --> 00:13:55.059
The most important thing was to preserve the location and position of the stadium.

00:13:56.552 --> 00:13:59.974
So the new stadium is positioned in exactly the same place as the old one.

00:14:03.777 --> 00:14:04.757
Why is this so important?

00:14:05.057 --> 00:14:08.139
Because people have become accustomed to the image of this building in the city.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:09.080
And above all,

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:10.441
They've adopted everyone's habits.

00:14:10.441 --> 00:14:12.602
always take the same route to get to the stadium.

00:14:15.042 --> 00:14:15.282
And that,

00:14:15.342 --> 00:14:17.283
It was very important to keep it too.

00:14:20.023 --> 00:14:20.363
In addition,

00:14:20.403 --> 00:14:24.344
The stadium is one of the three elements that create unity in the structure of the city.

00:14:24.664 --> 00:14:26.985
We leave from the Budapest Arena,

00:14:27.745 --> 00:14:29.045
then the garden of statues,

00:14:29.565 --> 00:14:30.186
the dromos,

00:14:30.346 --> 00:14:31.066
as it's called here,

00:14:31.866 --> 00:14:33.386
And we finally arrive at the Pushkas stadium.

00:14:38.011 --> 00:14:45.079
The perfect alignment of the enclosure with the statue garden and the Budapest arena was an essential prerequisite for the builders.

00:14:48.343 --> 00:14:54.530
The architect then had to imagine what this new stadium should look like so that the Hungarian people could identify with it.

00:15:01.964 --> 00:15:06.808
We needed to find characteristic elements of the stadium that could be saved from the old one.

00:15:09.289 --> 00:15:11.591
Our goal was to incorporate them into the new one,

00:15:12.311 --> 00:15:14.953
so that they integrate perfectly in an ordinary way.

00:15:14.993 --> 00:15:16.874
organic to our new enclosure.

00:15:20.475 --> 00:15:22.136
During the demolition of the old stadium,

00:15:22.777 --> 00:15:25.618
It was therefore decided to keep only one original element.

00:15:27.319 --> 00:15:33.942
The brick building that formerly housed the press center and which can be recognized in many archive photos.

00:15:38.555 --> 00:15:41.217
This building remains as the sole vestige of the past.

00:15:41.897 --> 00:15:44.499
in the middle of the construction site of a new, ultra-modern stadium.

00:15:48.721 --> 00:15:49.442
In the old stadium,

00:15:49.443 --> 00:15:51.183
the tower served as a press center.

00:15:52.063 --> 00:15:53.925
And in the next stadium,

00:15:53.985 --> 00:15:55.566
We're going to give it a new function.

00:15:57.087 --> 00:15:59.308
The museum will be housed in this tower.

00:16:01.129 --> 00:16:03.070
We want to keep this building in its original form.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:05.531
both outdoors and indoors.

00:16:06.811 --> 00:16:07.112
Actually,

00:16:07.192 --> 00:16:10.933
We wanted to keep it because it gives an excellent image of 1950s architecture.

00:16:11.814 --> 00:16:15.795
This perfectly illustrates the political climate of the time when plans for such a building were drawn up.

00:16:16.656 --> 00:16:19.057
This is what is called the socialist-realist style.

00:16:19.717 --> 00:16:22.278
And that fits well with the function of the museum we envisioned.

00:16:25.247 --> 00:16:30.930
The Hungarian architect also wanted to draw inspiration from the old stadium when designing the exterior of the new venue.

00:16:38.934 --> 00:16:41.396
The old stadium had a very striking feature,

00:16:41.816 --> 00:16:45.438
the pillars of the staircases that provided access to all levels of the stands.

00:16:47.859 --> 00:16:49.300
In each photo taken of the stadium,

00:16:49.301 --> 00:16:51.681
You can clearly see these pillars and especially the patterns that...

00:16:51.721 --> 00:16:53.862
which allowed one to see outside towards the city.

00:16:56.064 --> 00:16:58.065
It was a kind of very fine mesh,

00:16:58.345 --> 00:16:58.886
Made of concrete.

00:17:02.648 --> 00:17:06.451
The façade of the new stadium is therefore composed of 36 stairwells,

00:17:07.071 --> 00:17:09.012
distributed evenly around the stadium.

00:17:11.234 --> 00:17:17.818
All are covered with a concrete wall open to the outside and designed according to the same patterns as those of the old stadium.

00:17:21.607 --> 00:17:23.148
But even if the result appears identical,

00:17:23.829 --> 00:17:26.251
The structure is actually completely different.

00:17:29.873 --> 00:17:30.434
At the time,

00:17:31.154 --> 00:17:37.859
Specialized workers had built and assembled hundreds of small components on site with impressive precision.

00:17:40.101 --> 00:17:41.562
For the new Pushkas Arena,

00:17:42.283 --> 00:17:46.326
The designers found a much more ingenious and easier-to-implement solution.

00:17:48.719 --> 00:17:52.181
Each pillar is actually made up of about ten prefabricated panels.

00:17:52.681 --> 00:17:55.883
hoisted using a crane and slid directly into a steel rail.

00:18:00.766 --> 00:18:02.707
By preserving these motifs from the past,

00:18:03.427 --> 00:18:08.290
The Pouchkas Arena perpetuates the history of the people's stadium and can make all Hungarians proud.

00:18:13.553 --> 00:18:15.774
The Hungarian people loved the old stadium very much.

00:18:16.015 --> 00:18:17.175
We were all very attached to it.

00:18:19.517 --> 00:18:20.217
The biggest challenge,

00:18:20.297 --> 00:18:22.879
It was about figuring out how to make people love the new stadium.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.581
How could he possibly take the very special place that the old one held?

00:18:30.704 --> 00:18:31.745
After 4 years of work,

00:18:32.385 --> 00:18:33.586
The stadium is finally finished.

00:18:35.603 --> 00:18:38.165
The spectators immediately embraced their new cathedral.

00:18:39.386 --> 00:18:40.927
Thanks to its architectural features,

00:18:41.748 --> 00:18:43.309
It reminds them of the old enclosure.

00:18:54.879 --> 00:18:55.399
At only 9 years old,

00:18:55.439 --> 00:18:56.359
900 kilometers,

00:18:57.220 --> 00:19:01.842
The Bucharest National Arena is located in an extremely monitored seismic zone.

00:19:02.902 --> 00:19:07.084
Romania is the European Union country most vulnerable to earthquakes.

00:19:07.085 --> 00:19:11.285
In 1977,

00:19:11.926 --> 00:19:14.186
An unprecedented catastrophe has left its mark on people's minds.

00:19:15.955 --> 00:19:17.176
The Vrancea earthquake,

00:19:17.637 --> 00:19:20.119
with a magnitude of 7.2 on the Richter scale,

00:19:20.439 --> 00:19:21.440
struck Romania

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.181
Moldova and Bulgaria,

00:19:23.702 --> 00:19:26.104
causing more than 1,500 deaths and 11,000 injuries.

00:19:28.886 --> 00:19:31.108
To prevent a similar tragedy from happening again,

00:19:32.289 --> 00:19:37.153
The builders had to construct a framework capable of withstanding the most powerful earthquakes.

00:19:39.035 --> 00:19:43.158
The understanding between architects and engineers was fundamental to meeting this challenge.

00:19:47.084 --> 00:19:47.384
In my opinion,

00:19:48.605 --> 00:19:56.010
It was really important to talk about earthquake risks from the very beginning with the architects.

00:19:56.590 --> 00:20:01.033
I wanted to make sure that we would develop an optimal design from an architectural point of view.

00:20:01.033 --> 00:20:07.301
both architectural and structural.

00:20:07.381 --> 00:20:13.408
Good design is possible when the architect works with a structural engineer from the start of the project.

00:20:16.011 --> 00:20:18.973
Since the architect is responsible for both aesthetics and functionality,

00:20:19.473 --> 00:20:20.214
He has the last word.

00:20:22.775 --> 00:20:25.417
But when he listens to the structural engineer,

00:20:27.839 --> 00:20:31.841
He can adapt some of his ideas by taking his recommendations into account.

00:20:35.403 --> 00:20:43.755
Earthquake-resistant construction involves analyzing the interaction between the building and the ground and predicting the potential consequences of an earthquake.

00:20:44.917 --> 00:20:47.700
It then makes it possible to create a building that can withstand it.

00:20:56.368 --> 00:20:59.030
Seismic forces are inertial forces.

00:21:01.092 --> 00:21:04.414
This means that the forces arrive at every point of the structure.

00:21:06.355 --> 00:21:12.779
They need to be directed towards the walls to accumulate and then sent back to the ground.

00:21:16.022 --> 00:21:18.063
To ensure the stability of the structure,

00:21:18.804 --> 00:21:21.886
The engineers developed four specific anti-seismic features.

00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:28.170
Usually,

00:21:28.911 --> 00:21:31.813
A structure of this size is supported by 40 pillars.

00:21:33.234 --> 00:21:33.435
Here,

00:21:34.355 --> 00:21:36.997
The engineers added 80 additional pillars.

00:21:38.659 --> 00:21:39.640
6 seismic joints,

00:21:40.100 --> 00:21:41.601
distributed all around the perimeter,

00:21:41.701 --> 00:21:42.502
have been added.

00:21:44.083 --> 00:21:47.326
The 6 sub-parts can then move independently of each other.

00:21:47.906 --> 00:21:49.808
without damaging the entire structure.

00:21:55.191 --> 00:21:59.274
The engineers also built reinforcing walls perpendicular to the stands,

00:21:59.795 --> 00:22:03.137
distributed all around the stadium along the axis of each of the 120 pillars.

00:22:05.079 --> 00:22:06.500
To complete the system,

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:09.882
a wall parallel to the stands goes around the perimeter of the enclosure.

00:22:12.804 --> 00:22:13.085
Finally,

00:22:13.725 --> 00:22:14.886
below the upper tiers,

00:22:15.647 --> 00:22:18.849
Support walls have been put in place to reinforce the structure.

00:22:25.606 --> 00:22:27.930
Using conventional construction methods,

00:22:28.711 --> 00:22:31.776
The upper row of the stands is shaped like a step.

00:22:36.131 --> 00:22:36.351
Here,

00:22:36.592 --> 00:22:38.133
when viewed from the ground,

00:22:38.913 --> 00:22:40.314
the top row is flat.

00:22:42.035 --> 00:22:43.677
This is a unique characteristic.

00:22:44.537 --> 00:22:46.839
I find it very aesthetically pleasing that it's straight.

00:22:48.560 --> 00:22:49.461
As an architect,

00:22:49.781 --> 00:22:50.922
I think it's really beautiful.

00:22:51.422 --> 00:22:53.423
But it didn't come from a designer's idea.

00:22:53.904 --> 00:23:00.488
This was necessary to ensure it was as rigid as possible and could withstand the threat of earthquakes.

00:23:05.947 --> 00:23:14.433
Architects and engineers therefore designed and integrated as many solutions as possible to strengthen the structure and make it less vulnerable to earthquakes.

00:23:16.114 --> 00:23:19.616
Extraordinary equipment for an extraordinary site.

00:23:31.124 --> 00:23:31.824
In Budapest,

00:23:32.545 --> 00:23:34.806
The manufacturers had to face another challenge.

00:23:35.787 --> 00:23:42.391
Find a formwork system to build the enclosure columns in record time and in complete safety.

00:23:51.056 --> 00:23:52.958
To support the steel roof structure,

00:23:53.538 --> 00:23:55.399
36 pillars with variable geometry are installed.

00:23:56.099 --> 00:23:58.640
structures 45 meters high must be built.

00:23:59.620 --> 00:24:00.120
But above all,

00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:02.561
These pillars must be completed simultaneously.

00:24:03.241 --> 00:24:08.703
because the arrival of an exceptional crane from Belgium to lift the roof elements is scheduled.

00:24:10.283 --> 00:24:14.004
For the engineers and workers, a race against time then begins.

00:24:15.945 --> 00:24:22.406
They will use a specific formwork that allows these gigantic columns to be built simultaneously and at the same pace.

00:24:34.739 --> 00:24:37.341
The principle is to advance the construction of the pillar.

00:24:37.741 --> 00:24:38.562
step by step,

00:24:38.762 --> 00:24:39.463
from bottom to top.

00:24:41.344 --> 00:24:42.085
To achieve this,

00:24:42.665 --> 00:24:45.267
They chose to use a three-level formwork system.

00:24:47.349 --> 00:24:52.193
The first two floors of the pillar must first be built using a classic formwork technique.

00:24:54.735 --> 00:24:55.375
From there,

00:24:56.115 --> 00:25:00.197
We can then install a system perfectly adapted to the height and shape of the pillar.

00:25:01.237 --> 00:25:03.898
Three platforms are used by the workers to carry out the work.

00:25:07.839 --> 00:25:11.680
The lower platform is used for finishing and cleaning work.

00:25:14.721 --> 00:25:20.143
The middle platform is where the formwork elements are located to build the upper level.

00:25:21.319 --> 00:25:25.301
The last platform allows workers to pour concrete into the formwork.

00:25:29.804 --> 00:25:30.825
Once the level is completed,

00:25:31.485 --> 00:25:33.946
The entire system is raised to the next level.

00:25:39.650 --> 00:25:41.030
Thanks to the adaptable formwork,

00:25:41.371 --> 00:25:43.472
which can be retracted up to 75 cm,

00:25:44.312 --> 00:25:46.393
the wall takes on the desired thickness or shape.

00:25:51.367 --> 00:25:52.748
The levels can be linked together in this way,

00:25:53.389 --> 00:25:56.771
while respecting the shape of the pillars envisioned by the architects.

00:25:58.373 --> 00:25:58.853
In total,

00:25:59.514 --> 00:26:00.855
There are 10 levels per pillar.

00:26:03.797 --> 00:26:07.360
To meet the deadlines and erect the 36 pillars before the crane arrives,

00:26:08.101 --> 00:26:10.663
250 formworks of this type were required.

00:26:16.507 --> 00:26:17.929
And to make matters more complicated,

00:26:18.269 --> 00:26:20.491
in this country where the temperature range is significant,

00:26:21.159 --> 00:26:24.149
The concrete pouring always had to take place at the same time of day.

00:26:27.460 --> 00:26:31.483
It was necessary to ensure that the surface of each pillar was a uniform grey colour.

00:26:32.424 --> 00:26:32.765
For that,

00:26:32.825 --> 00:26:36.008
The concrete formwork had to be put in place at roughly the same time of day.

00:26:37.049 --> 00:26:37.329
Otherwise,

00:26:37.429 --> 00:26:40.712
because evaporation mechanisms differ depending on the time of day,

00:26:40.993 --> 00:26:43.755
The color of the concrete could have been different from one level to another.

00:26:45.957 --> 00:26:50.502
The use of this exceptional construction device offers several advantages.

00:26:55.937 --> 00:26:59.720
The main advantage of these two systems is that when you are on fairly high floors,

00:27:00.080 --> 00:27:00.781
in the fourth,

00:27:00.861 --> 00:27:01.961
fifth or sixth,

00:27:02.382 --> 00:27:04.443
We don't need to separate them at each stage.

00:27:04.923 --> 00:27:06.264
They can be hoisted together,

00:27:06.484 --> 00:27:07.045
all at once.

00:27:07.665 --> 00:27:13.470
thanks to the crane.

00:27:13.510 --> 00:27:14.671
Another important advantage,

00:27:14.711 --> 00:27:19.395
It's a safe system that allows workers to work in a secure environment.

00:27:19.895 --> 00:27:22.557
protected by a fence at a very high altitude.

00:27:25.019 --> 00:27:25.439
And finally,

00:27:25.459 --> 00:27:27.301
The crane's usage time is short.

00:27:27.481 --> 00:27:30.543
It's quite quick to simply upgrade the system from one level to the next.

00:27:35.667 --> 00:27:37.988
The pillars are therefore not built one after the other,

00:27:38.489 --> 00:27:39.429
but all at the same time.

00:27:42.571 --> 00:27:45.693
This system allows progress on the different pillars simultaneously.

00:27:47.133 --> 00:27:48.935
While waiting for the concrete to dry on one level,

00:27:49.735 --> 00:27:51.976
The process is then carried out at the next level on a neighboring pillar.

00:27:55.158 --> 00:27:55.398
So,

00:27:56.519 --> 00:27:59.160
The 36 pillars were completed in just one year.

00:27:59.921 --> 00:28:03.122
just in time for the crane to hoist the imposing steel roof.

00:28:14.783 --> 00:28:15.844
At an exceptional stage,

00:28:16.525 --> 00:28:17.606
exceptional project.

00:28:24.191 --> 00:28:25.392
And what if at the Pouchkas Arena,

00:28:25.673 --> 00:28:28.435
36 pillars were built directly on site,

00:28:32.659 --> 00:28:33.800
at the National Arena,

00:28:34.740 --> 00:28:36.962
The teams had to erect 120 of them.

00:28:42.691 --> 00:28:45.033
They poured the concrete into formwork on site.

00:28:54.959 --> 00:28:55.399
But for the...

00:28:55.459 --> 00:28:57.179
40 columns that will support the roof,

00:28:57.960 --> 00:29:01.201
They were built more than 1500 km from Bucharest.

00:29:01.701 --> 00:29:03.061
in Neumark, Germany,

00:29:03.581 --> 00:29:05.002
then transported by heavy goods vehicle.

00:29:14.204 --> 00:29:17.385
But building all the parts in Germany was too complex and expensive.

00:29:20.446 --> 00:29:21.726
So, the German architects,

00:29:21.786 --> 00:29:23.907
in collaboration with Romanian architects,

00:29:24.751 --> 00:29:25.752
had another idea.

00:29:32.896 --> 00:29:37.359
Imagine that we have built a huge rigid tent like a circus tent.

00:29:37.980 --> 00:29:39.321
It's a practical solution.

00:29:40.401 --> 00:29:44.804
A large tent, 50 meters long and 50 meters wide.

00:29:49.666 --> 00:29:50.487
In this tent,

00:29:51.227 --> 00:29:52.688
The parts were prefabricated.

00:29:53.088 --> 00:29:55.389
which were then stored for a certain period of time.

00:29:59.690 --> 00:30:00.751
When they were ready,

00:30:01.451 --> 00:30:06.393
They were brought to the construction site and stored until they were installed.

00:30:12.199 --> 00:30:12.760
The stands,

00:30:13.040 --> 00:30:13.800
the stairs,

00:30:13.920 --> 00:30:14.461
the ramps,

00:30:14.841 --> 00:30:19.645
The small posts and even the transverse wall were built directly on the construction site.

00:30:24.569 --> 00:30:24.929
Yet,

00:30:25.649 --> 00:30:29.312
The constraints imposed by seismic risks complicate the task of the teams.

00:30:29.913 --> 00:30:31.394
Because in order to withstand earthquakes,

00:30:32.014 --> 00:30:34.897
The prefabricated parts need to be larger.

00:30:35.457 --> 00:30:36.378
therefore heavier.

00:30:43.340 --> 00:30:45.101
With small prefabricated elements,

00:30:45.161 --> 00:30:46.442
Cranes can be used.

00:30:47.043 --> 00:30:50.165
These are the same cranes that are used for other tasks on the construction site.

00:30:50.446 --> 00:30:52.487
For large elements or roof elements,

00:30:52.808 --> 00:30:54.529
We use specific cranes,

00:30:54.749 --> 00:30:56.851
which have greater load capacities.

00:30:57.251 --> 00:30:58.953
When building with prefabricated materials,

00:30:59.413 --> 00:31:03.636
The equipment used to transport and install the components plays a fundamental role.

00:31:03.977 --> 00:31:05.478
because the loads are very heavy.

00:31:08.520 --> 00:31:11.223
The design of the prefabricated parts must be final.

00:31:12.127 --> 00:31:14.790
because it is impossible to modify an element once it has been installed.

00:31:20.075 --> 00:31:24.540
This requires extremely rigorous planning and meticulous organization.

00:31:25.161 --> 00:31:26.982
but it has many advantages.

00:31:33.661 --> 00:31:36.103
Construction time is much faster.

00:31:36.843 --> 00:31:38.264
The quality is perfect.

00:31:40.766 --> 00:31:43.387
No further treatment is needed.

00:31:43.648 --> 00:31:45.769
cleaning or smoothing with plastic.

00:31:47.111 --> 00:31:51.756
We don't need to wait for the concrete to harden before moving on to the next step.

00:31:56.442 --> 00:32:00.427
We can continue to build the different parts as we go along.

00:32:03.429 --> 00:32:10.075
It's really satisfying to see how quickly these Lego pieces were assembled and clicked together properly.

00:32:11.836 --> 00:32:13.398
Everything worked perfectly.

00:32:19.483 --> 00:32:21.464
Once all the prefabricated elements are installed,

00:32:22.085 --> 00:32:23.726
The structure needs to be fitted with a roof.

00:32:27.051 --> 00:32:29.999
To avoid weakening the structure in the face of an earthquake,

00:32:30.500 --> 00:32:33.588
The engineers opted for an extremely lightweight cover.

00:32:45.320 --> 00:32:46.601
The lighter your roof,

00:32:47.021 --> 00:32:48.902
The more it will withstand earthquakes.

00:32:50.683 --> 00:32:56.187
And that's also how a lightweight structure is stronger than any beam system.

00:32:56.307 --> 00:32:57.428
megabeams or other structures

00:32:57.908 --> 00:32:59.049
used in a stadium.

00:33:04.355 --> 00:33:06.478
And to ensure the roof is as strong as possible,

00:33:08.741 --> 00:33:11.084
The engineers installed a reinforcement system.

00:33:11.724 --> 00:33:12.565
steel cables.

00:33:16.689 --> 00:33:22.154
The roof rests partly on the bleachers and is connected to them by 8 pairs of cables in a cross shape.

00:33:23.314 --> 00:33:24.255
Since there are several of them,

00:33:24.295 --> 00:33:25.376
if one pair is missing,

00:33:25.796 --> 00:33:26.757
There's always enough.

00:33:28.679 --> 00:33:30.660
But the key is to minimize dead weight,

00:33:30.961 --> 00:33:31.761
the weight of the roof,

00:33:32.202 --> 00:33:34.383
so that the acceleration is not destructive.

00:33:39.908 --> 00:33:41.869
As in many stadiums across the globe,

00:33:41.889 --> 00:33:43.831
Architects and engineers were also involved in the creation of these structures.

00:33:43.831 --> 00:33:46.013
opted for a bicycle wheel roof system.

00:33:56.625 --> 00:34:04.033
The trick is to find a system that prevents the forces acting on lightweight structures from simply being transferred into the ground.

00:34:04.493 --> 00:34:05.875
but to be counterbalanced.

00:34:09.192 --> 00:34:13.235
Systems called bicycle wheel systems are now very commonly used.

00:34:17.057 --> 00:34:19.958
That's what we did for the roof structure of the Bucharest stadium.

00:34:21.259 --> 00:34:23.520
It's the same principle, but more complex.

00:34:24.161 --> 00:34:25.901
And that's what we decided to use.

00:34:29.515 --> 00:34:32.617
To be able to have both a fixed and a retractable part,

00:34:33.317 --> 00:34:35.779
The roof of the national arena is very elaborate.

00:34:41.242 --> 00:34:41.462
Here,

00:34:42.342 --> 00:34:44.543
Two bicycle wheel systems were combined,

00:34:45.064 --> 00:34:48.265
one for the fixed part and one for the retractable part.

00:34:51.587 --> 00:34:52.768
For the fixed part of the roof,

00:34:53.528 --> 00:34:58.731
The 40 columns connected by 18-meter-long beams form the rim of the first wheel.

00:34:59.771 --> 00:35:01.633
This is called a compression ring.

00:35:05.595 --> 00:35:10.237
A system of taut cables connected to the center of the roof structure represents the spokes.

00:35:10.918 --> 00:35:13.039
They will be attached to the rim of the second wheel.

00:35:15.140 --> 00:35:15.540
Again,

00:35:16.200 --> 00:35:18.882
Cables are stretched to the center of the second bicycle wheel.

00:35:21.059 --> 00:35:24.402
The hub of the second wheel is the central point of the entire system.

00:35:25.443 --> 00:35:29.246
It's a large 40-ton steel piece that houses the retractable roof.

00:35:33.769 --> 00:35:35.451
To ensure the entire roof is balanced,

00:35:36.231 --> 00:35:38.793
Vertical tubes were installed in the center of the two wheels.

00:35:41.896 --> 00:35:48.281
Cables from the central piece pass over the steel tubes and attach to the beams of the compression ring.

00:35:50.523 --> 00:35:50.803
So,

00:35:51.544 --> 00:35:56.327
Two wheels with very distinct functions are suspended thanks to this wiring system.

00:36:04.633 --> 00:36:07.515
But the most striking feature of the national arena's roof,

00:36:08.215 --> 00:36:11.838
It's the fully automated removable system of its retractable roof.

00:36:16.827 --> 00:36:18.068
This technological marvel,

00:36:18.388 --> 00:36:22.389
which spans 9,000 square meters and weighs over 25,000 tons,

00:36:22.970 --> 00:36:24.590
It installs in just 8 minutes.

00:36:37.416 --> 00:36:39.877
The roof covering is stored in a large box,

00:36:40.377 --> 00:36:41.997
which is called the video cube,

00:36:42.638 --> 00:36:44.498
located at a height of 42 meters.

00:36:47.863 --> 00:36:51.164
It is equipped with 4 giant screens and several speakers for sound.

00:37:00.868 --> 00:37:03.429
The box can be lowered to the ground for maintenance.

00:37:13.233 --> 00:37:16.234
Dan Radou takes us inside this extraordinary structure.

00:37:27.707 --> 00:37:29.089
So here we are in the video cube.

00:37:31.211 --> 00:37:32.092
It's a giant box,

00:37:32.093 --> 00:37:32.752
It's gigantic.

00:37:33.833 --> 00:37:38.858
Here we have the four electric motors that allow the video cube to move up and down.

00:37:38.859 --> 00:37:41.421
All these cables are electrical.

00:37:41.461 --> 00:37:44.823
Electrical cables provide power for all the installations found there.

00:37:49.206 --> 00:37:52.048
The surface area of ​​these video walls is 36 square meters.

00:37:53.989 --> 00:37:58.352
And the power of the sound broadcast throughout the stadium can reach 70,000 watts.

00:38:17.378 --> 00:38:19.939
At the controls of this ultra-sophisticated, state-of-the-art system,

00:38:20.699 --> 00:38:21.500
Katalin Soare,

00:38:21.960 --> 00:38:23.080
Director of Operations.

00:38:25.422 --> 00:38:25.682
Here,

00:38:26.002 --> 00:38:27.222
We are in the control room.

00:38:27.903 --> 00:38:30.264
And we find ourselves facing the two control panels.

00:38:31.104 --> 00:38:34.005
One for the roof and one for the video cube.

00:38:35.166 --> 00:38:36.226
The two screens are linked.

00:38:38.948 --> 00:38:39.609
On this one,

00:38:40.389 --> 00:38:44.353
We receive the data transmitted by the weather station on the retractable roof.

00:38:45.333 --> 00:38:48.856
You can see the speed in kilometers per hour.

00:38:49.357 --> 00:38:51.018
the temperature.

00:38:51.659 --> 00:38:53.040
Depending on the wind speed,

00:38:53.860 --> 00:38:55.422
The system goes into safe mode.

00:38:57.904 --> 00:39:00.286
If the wind exceeds 20 km/h, for example,

00:39:00.766 --> 00:39:02.668
The station is blocking the roof mechanism.

00:39:03.348 --> 00:39:04.529
which can no longer be activated.

00:39:05.470 --> 00:39:06.771
The blockage lasts 60 minutes.

00:39:07.472 --> 00:39:08.072
At that moment,

00:39:08.193 --> 00:39:09.074
if the wind has calmed down,

00:39:09.554 --> 00:39:13.038
The mechanism is unlocked.

00:39:16.762 --> 00:39:17.943
To proceed with the opening,

00:39:18.544 --> 00:39:20.626
The video cube needs to be lowered by 8 meters.

00:39:29.783 --> 00:39:29.963
Then,

00:39:30.103 --> 00:39:34.365
Carts transport and unfold the membrane onto steel cables which,

00:39:34.566 --> 00:39:36.547
in addition to supporting the weight of the structure,

00:39:37.007 --> 00:39:37.827
act as a rail.

00:39:42.330 --> 00:39:45.091
This system is fully automated and secure.

00:39:48.413 --> 00:39:50.534
When you proceed with opening...

00:39:53.447 --> 00:39:57.810
You can see the pressure level and real-time position of each engine,

00:40:00.012 --> 00:40:01.373
whether they are late or not.

00:40:02.654 --> 00:40:07.577
Each motor is independent and their position is shown as a percentage of distance traveled.

00:40:18.899 --> 00:40:19.640
Once in place,

00:40:20.481 --> 00:40:24.485
A system of hydraulic jacks attaches the membrane and puts the cables under tension.

00:40:27.988 --> 00:40:29.970
The roof is then perfectly rigid.

00:40:41.893 --> 00:40:42.413
At the end,

00:40:43.054 --> 00:40:49.099
The system automatically stops the carriages of the 32 motors to secure the entire mechanism.

00:40:53.202 --> 00:40:53.563
And we,

00:40:53.663 --> 00:40:55.064
from our control room,

00:40:56.225 --> 00:41:00.428
We can verify that each engine is properly stopped on our monitors.

00:41:13.344 --> 00:41:14.664
Although extremely complex,

00:41:15.324 --> 00:41:19.426
This system appears incredibly simple when you watch it unfold.

00:41:25.667 --> 00:41:27.708
The roof resembles a kind of giant umbrella,

00:41:27.868 --> 00:41:28.348
very light,

00:41:28.928 --> 00:41:31.729
which covers the enclosure and protects the spectators,

00:41:32.129 --> 00:41:33.910
but without giving them the impression of being locked up.

00:41:45.207 --> 00:41:45.887
In Budapest,

00:41:46.588 --> 00:41:48.909
The Puskas Arena is also equipped with a roof,

00:41:49.529 --> 00:41:51.189
built using state-of-the-art techniques.

00:41:58.913 --> 00:42:01.214
Unlike the old stadium, which was completely open,

00:42:01.774 --> 00:42:03.915
The stands today are completely covered.

00:42:07.615 --> 00:42:13.960
One of the biggest challenges for the engineers was to manufacture the immense roof that covers the entirety of the stadium's stands.

00:42:15.902 --> 00:42:20.946
A 10,000-tonne metal structure resting atop the stadium's 36 stairwells,

00:42:21.687 --> 00:42:25.771
creating a gigantic cantilever 90 meters long.

00:42:30.815 --> 00:42:34.118
The elements that make up the roof are first manufactured on the ground.

00:42:36.487 --> 00:42:37.207
Around the stadium,

00:42:38.128 --> 00:42:40.369
It's a veritable giant Meccano set that has been organized.

00:42:40.889 --> 00:42:44.410
composed of hundreds of metal tubes that workers must assemble.

00:42:53.854 --> 00:42:56.695
The roof is divided into 36 identical segments.

00:42:58.596 --> 00:43:03.118
Each segment consists of three distinct elements which are first assembled separately.

00:43:08.916 --> 00:43:15.821
They are then hoisted one by one to the top of the stairwell and fixed to each other to obtain the total length of the cantilever.

00:43:28.370 --> 00:43:30.031
From the moment the first beam is installed,

00:43:30.592 --> 00:43:34.094
This high-risk operation required the use of exceptional resources.

00:43:49.632 --> 00:43:58.402
This structure, composed of three metal elements, reaches 80 to 90 meters in length and weighs more than 250 tons.

00:43:59.343 --> 00:44:00.824
To lift such a structure,

00:44:01.425 --> 00:44:05.510
It was necessary to bring in a crane of which there are only 8 examples in Europe.

00:44:06.771 --> 00:44:11.212
capable of lifting 1000 tonnes and the load curve is 130 metres.

00:44:13.513 --> 00:44:21.235
The crane will therefore lift the three elements that make up each segment of the framework and allow them to be fixed to each other at the top.

00:44:22.575 --> 00:44:27.036
This operation will have to be repeated on all 36 stairwells of the stadium.

00:44:27.617 --> 00:44:28.137
In total,

00:44:28.457 --> 00:44:31.318
That makes 36 times three elements to hoist up there.

00:44:34.458 --> 00:44:36.579
Barnabas Sighetti leads us to the top of the stadium.

00:44:36.579 --> 00:44:36.839
stadium,

00:44:37.359 --> 00:44:40.641
at the point where the metal framework and the concrete meet.

00:44:45.564 --> 00:44:47.546
The biggest technical challenge of the project,

00:44:47.626 --> 00:44:49.167
It's this roof structure.

00:44:49.707 --> 00:44:53.849
The length of the roof varies between 80 and 90 meters depending on its position.

00:44:54.310 --> 00:44:55.150
It's very, very long.

00:44:55.691 --> 00:44:59.733
This corresponds to the size of a football pitch and the points of support on which...

00:44:59.833 --> 00:45:14.691
The structural elements rest relatively close to each other, and therefore the forces they must withstand are truly enormous. In the first phase of design, the engineers considered using traditional solutions to secure the stadium roof.

00:45:14.711 --> 00:45:16.832
stadium with classic steel components.

00:45:17.892 --> 00:45:20.413
But they found that with this type of system,

00:45:21.014 --> 00:45:29.777
the strength of the framework was not guaranteed and cracks could appear in the areas subjected to the greatest stresses.

00:45:35.223 --> 00:45:36.904
To support the 10,000 tonnes of the roof,

00:45:37.585 --> 00:45:40.246
The engineers resorted to a novel solution.

00:45:41.546 --> 00:45:48.450
Each of the 36 segments that make up the framework rests on 4 supports placed at the top of each stairwell.

00:45:50.871 --> 00:45:56.113
It is at the level of these four steel pieces that all the stresses due to the weight of the framework are distributed.

00:45:58.613 --> 00:45:59.233
At this location,

00:46:00.014 --> 00:46:03.235
conventional fixings would likely fail with such a long overhang.

00:46:04.435 --> 00:46:07.616
The designers therefore invented a system of invisible cables.

00:46:09.817 --> 00:46:15.918
Eight groups of metal cables are attached to each plate and are then pulled downwards under tension.

00:46:18.355 --> 00:46:20.396
They thus recover the stresses of the framework,

00:46:21.016 --> 00:46:23.797
then they are fixed to the inside of the stairwell walls.

00:46:25.777 --> 00:46:26.257
In total,

00:46:26.857 --> 00:46:28.378
to support the enormous weight of the roof,

00:46:29.278 --> 00:46:36.640
There are nearly 11,000 cables that attach to supports placed at the top of the stairwells and pass through the concrete walls of the Pouchkas Arena.

00:46:39.101 --> 00:46:39.721
On the construction site,

00:46:40.521 --> 00:46:46.143
The workers are stretching the long cables that can be seen in some places of the stadium already embedded in the concrete of the facade.

00:46:54.164 --> 00:46:56.044
This project is a major challenge for us.

00:46:56.985 --> 00:47:00.306
A public building of this size had never been built in Hungary before.

00:47:01.166 --> 00:47:03.106
We're talking about an enormous size.

00:47:03.927 --> 00:47:04.507
Can you imagine?

00:47:04.847 --> 00:47:10.849
The amount of cable incorporated into the stadium would allow Budapest to be connected to Barcelona or London.

00:47:14.810 --> 00:47:15.310
In total,

00:47:16.190 --> 00:47:18.071
The stadium was built in 32 months.

00:47:19.191 --> 00:47:21.152
And the schedule was scrupulously followed.

00:47:23.632 --> 00:47:26.353
We inaugurated the stadium ten days ahead of schedule.

00:47:26.994 --> 00:47:28.694
We wanted to do it on November 25th.

00:47:29.454 --> 00:47:32.495
November 25th is the anniversary of Hungary's most important match.

00:47:32.515 --> 00:47:34.236
In 1953,

00:47:34.476 --> 00:47:37.717
The Hungarian team has beaten the English team six times at Wembley.

00:47:38.778 --> 00:47:42.643
It was a historic victory and our team was led by Puskas.

00:47:43.644 --> 00:47:46.808
We would have liked to inaugurate the stadium on the anniversary of this event.

00:47:47.309 --> 00:47:50.472
but the UEFA competition calendar did not allow it.

00:47:51.093 --> 00:47:52.675
We were in the qualifying period for...

00:47:52.675 --> 00:47:56.719
of the European Championship and we had to adapt to the international competition calendar.

00:47:57.199 --> 00:48:04.746
November 15th was the only available day and we had to accelerate our schedule and finish the work 10 days ahead of the planned deadline.

00:48:06.588 --> 00:48:09.951
For these men who participated in the construction of this temple of football,

00:48:10.671 --> 00:48:13.074
The completion of this major project is generating a lot of emotion.

00:48:18.371 --> 00:48:19.292
We are very happy.

00:48:19.972 --> 00:48:21.912
It was a pleasure to work on this.

00:48:22.172 --> 00:48:23.753
It wasn't even really a job,

00:48:24.213 --> 00:48:25.814
but something that was important to us.

00:48:26.754 --> 00:48:31.095
Everyone who participated in it considers it one of the most important projects of their life.

00:48:36.677 --> 00:48:37.698
And for the spectators,

00:48:38.298 --> 00:48:40.859
The new Puskas Arena is a real success.

00:48:42.323 --> 00:48:46.364
The traffic routes are open to the outside and connect the stadium to the city.

00:48:50.346 --> 00:48:55.747
Many facilities have been improved to welcome visitors and offer them a unique experience.

00:48:58.868 --> 00:48:59.609
On match nights,

00:49:00.369 --> 00:49:02.470
The stadium can light up in different colors.

00:49:03.530 --> 00:49:04.330
When Hungary plays,

00:49:04.770 --> 00:49:06.691
It is the national flag that colors the facade.

00:49:07.051 --> 00:49:08.912
and strengthens the fervor of the supporters.

00:49:35.559 --> 00:49:40.648
The National Arena in Bucharest and the Pouchkas Arena in Budapest have managed to reinvent themselves,

00:49:41.189 --> 00:49:45.898
while respecting the legendary characteristics of the old enclosures that have now been destroyed.

00:49:49.633 --> 00:49:51.954
It is a very important place for the inhabitants of Bucharest.

00:49:53.555 --> 00:49:55.516
Not only is it the largest stadium in Romania,

00:49:56.497 --> 00:49:58.118
But above all, it's the most beautiful stadium in the country.

00:50:00.039 --> 00:50:03.201
And I am very proud to have this opportunity to be here and to work here.

00:50:09.715 --> 00:50:14.019
We are pleased to have built a new stadium that truly resembles the previous one.

00:50:14.239 --> 00:50:15.260
the people's stadium.

00:50:16.221 --> 00:50:18.243
By looking at and comparing the two stages,

00:50:18.583 --> 00:50:20.325
The resemblance is striking.

00:50:21.046 --> 00:50:24.729
We are really pleased that people like it and that this performance is

00:50:25.169 --> 00:50:25.870
100% Hungarian.

00:50:26.511 --> 00:50:29.113
It's good that we stayed within our budget and deadlines.

00:50:34.683 --> 00:50:40.386
These two 21st-century arenas can now write a new chapter in their country's history.

